From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: skip the prefix ownership check on PS5/PS4 too.

create_dir() already skips its st_uid test under __PROSPERO__, with the note
"one user; its file systems do not keep unix owners". create_server_dir() makes
the same test against the prefix itself and was left unguarded, so it fires
whenever the prefix was not written by the running user.

This is the previously validated PS4 patch 0112 from ps4-gladius, carried
forward onto the ABI-v4 base.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -1154,8 +1154,10 @@ static char *create_server_dir( int force )
         fatal_error( "open %s: %s\n", config_dir, strerror( errno ));
     if (fstat( config_dir_fd, &st ) == -1)
         fatal_error( "stat %s: %s\n", config_dir, strerror( errno ));
+#ifndef __PROSPERO__  /* one user; PS4 filesystems do not preserve Unix owners */
     if (st.st_uid != getuid())
         fatal_error( "%s is not owned by you\n", config_dir );
+#endif
 
     /* create the base directory if needed */
